<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Æthelfrith of Northumbria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 616</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Æthelfrith, Æthelfrith of Bernicia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Æthelfrith was king of Bernicia from about 593 and, from about 604, also of Deira, uniting them as the first ruler of Northumbria. He defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Áedán mac Gabráin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> at Degsastan in 603 and the Britons at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a> around 615, but was killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raedwald-of-east-anglia">Rædwald of East Anglia</a> at the River Idle in 616. His sons later ruled Northumbria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="Æthelfrith of Northumbria" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Hel-hama · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Britain_peoples_circa_600.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
